<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    DEBUG ONLY. THIS MUST NEVER BE WHAT SHIPS.

    This file exists solely so a debug build can reach the NodeMCU water-level
    probe, which:

      - cannot do TLS, so it serves plain HTTP and nothing else, and
      - has a DHCP-assigned LAN address that changes between sessions, so its
        host is not known when this file is written.

    Those two facts together are why this is a blanket permit rather than a
    scoped one. Android's network-security-config matches <domain> entries as
    hostnames - exact, or by suffix with includeSubdomains - and has no syntax
    for an IP range. The previous version of the release config listed
    "10.0.0.0/8" and friends as <domain> values; those were treated as literal
    domain strings, matched nothing, and left base-config's
    cleartextTrafficPermitted="false" in force. That is what blocked the sensor
    request inside the app while the phone's browser reached the same URL
    fine.

    The release config in src/main stays strict and is NOT overridden by this.
    Resource merging picks the debug source set only for debug builds; see the
    note in src/main/res/xml/network_security_config.xml for what a release
    build would need instead.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" />
</network-security-config>
